  "changes": [
    "Curl and twist the spine independently of the incoming root roll; gather knees toward the chest with negative hip pitch, stagger the supporting hand and lead foot, and unfold the chest last. Reuse editable segment elasticity and the finite rise rebound.",
    "Use a 0.64-second ordinary get-up (previously 0.56); severe impacts add up to 0.4 seconds. Round the gait half-wave at the loaded passing step, fading to the unchanged ordinary gait after recovery.",
    "Hard wall or floor contacts settle onto a broad back or belly surface with relaxed limbs. Hold approximately 0.3\u20130.5 seconds once flat and quiet, then recover. Airborne travel remains physical; a bounded 1.6-second supported fallback prevents a wedged incident from holding forever.",
    "Preserve interrupted pose/spin for 0.24 seconds. On upward hops, brake the support-relative waist drift while preserving its initial derivative, preventing the curled chest from driving the waist back through the floor.",
    "Add Heavy wall, High fall and Knocked flat controls to the local review lab."
